se, and the stated expiry restrictions.\",\n  \"by\": \"Hamza (via web)\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"Q-4\",\n  \"question\": \"For contracted customer-order and allocation operations, how much of the described order lifecycle should be implemented beyond basic persistence of contract fields?\",\n  \"answer\": \"Apply the explicit order rules where exposed: customer changes/cancellation only before packing, duplicate-submission protection, suitable-stock allocation, and the stated allocation and back-order behavior.\",\n  \"by\": \"Hamza (via web)\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"Q-5\",\n  \"question\": \"How broad should the audit history be for contracted data changes? The request requires an audit trail and says records can be changed after the fact, but does not define the complete event set or immutability behavior.\",\n  \"answer\": \"Store actor and time for consequential changes and decisions exposed by contracted operations.\",\n  \"by\": \"Hamza (via web)\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"Q-6\",\n  \"question\": \"How long must audit events for consequential changes and decisions remain available?\",\n  \"answer\": \"Retain audit events without automatic expiry.\",\n  \"by\": \"Hamza (via web)\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"Q-7\",\n  \"question\": \"What should happen to the existing spreadsheet-based operational data when the API is introduced?\",\n  \"answer\": \"Do not migrate legacy data; start with records entered through the contracted API operations.\",\n  \"by\": \"Hamza (via web)\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"Q-8\",\n  \"question\": \"When the configured database is unavailable or invalid, what should the API do beyond the existing fail-fast behavior for a missing connection string?\",\n  \"answer\": \"Fail startup for invalid configuration and return the contract-defined server error for failed operations; never report a business operation as successful.\",\n  \"by\": \"Hamza (via web)\"\n }\n]\n</artifact>\n\n<artifact id=\"assumptions\" kind=\"assumptions\" sha=\"\">\n[\n {\n  \"fromDefault\": \"sign-in\",\n  \"fromQuestion\": \"Q2\",\n  \"fromSpan\": [\n   \"I-2\"\n  ],\n  \"id\": \"ASM-1\",\n  \"risk\": \"high\",\n  \"text\": \"What authentication integration is expected behind the contract's staff authorization-URL operation and the described customer sign-in? → assumed: Email and password, with a reset link by email; no social or single sign-on.\"\n },\n {\n  \"fromDefault\": \"data-migration\",\n  \"fromQuestion\": \"Q6\",\n  \"fromSpan\": [\n   \"I-3\"\n  ],\n  \"id\": \"ASM-2\",\n  \"risk\": \"high\",\n  \"text\": \"Should the API bring existing spreadsheet or paper-process data into the new persisted records, or start with no imported business data? → assumed: No; the system starts empty, with seed data for set-up.\"\n },\n {\n  \"fromDefault\": \"notifications\",\n  \"fromQuestion\": \"Q7\",\n  \"fromSpan\": [\n   \"I-2\",\n   \"I-3\"\n  ],\n  \"id\": \"ASM-3\",\n  \"risk\": \"high\",\n  \"text\": \"The request says readings arrive through a logger supplier's gateway and that alerts reach drivers, dispatchers, and Quality Officers, but does not identify the supplier, gateway authentication, or alert delivery channel. What should the API integrate with? → assumed: Email only, from fixed templates; no SMS or push.\"\n },\n {\n  \"fromQuestion\": \"Q8\",\n  \"fromSpan\": [\n   \"I-3\"\n  ],\n  \"id\": \"ASM-4\",\n  \"risk\": \"high\",\n  \"text\": \"What is the persisted unit meant by “handling unit” for temperature-budget history when part of a lot is split into different boxes or storage histories? → assumed: A separately tracked quantity or lot portion becomes a handling unit when its history diverges, such as when it is split into a different box.\"\n },\n {\n  \"fromQuestion\": \"Q9\",\n  \"fromSpan\": [\n   \"I-3\"\n  ],\n  \"id\": \"ASM-5\",\n  \"risk\": \"high\",\n  \"text\": \"How should the API ensure stock becomes Expired at the end of its expiry date and is removed from allocations, given that the API-side request does not specify a scheduler or other trigger? → assumed: Run an application-side scheduled check that updates expired stock, removes allocations, and records the resulting dispatcher alert.\"\n },\n {\n  \"fromDefault\": \"admin\",\n  \"fromQuestion\": \"Q11\",\n  \"fromSpan\": [\n   \"I-2\",\n   \"I-3\"\n  ],\n  \"id\": \"ASM-6\",\n  \"risk\": \"low\",\n  \"text\": \"The request makes order cut-off times and route safety margins configurable, with warehouse-specific working days and holidays, but does not say where those values are maintained. How should contracted operations obtain them? → assumed: Administrators work in the same app on admin-only screens; no separate back office.\"\n },\n {\n  \"fromQuestion\": \"Q-1\",\n  \"fromSpan\": [\n   \"I-1\"\n  ],\n  \"id\": \"ASM-7\",\n  \"risk\": \"low\",\n  \"text\": \"Should the existing root health response and Swagger/OpenAPI UI remain available alongside the contracted operations? → assumed: Keep the existing health response, OpenAPI document, and Swagger UI.\"\n },\n {\n  \"fromQuestion\": \"Q-4\",\n  \"fromSpan\": [\n   \"I-2\",\n   \"I-3\"\n  ],\n  \"id\": \"ASM-8\",\n  \"risk\": \"high\",\n  \"text\": \"How should the API establish that temperature readings are coming from the logger supplier's gateway, and which supplier integration details should it use? → assumed: Accept readings through the locked contract operation using gateway credentials/configuration supplied for deployment; do not add a vendor-specific client.\"\n },\n {\n  \"fromDefault\": \"sign-in\",\n  \"fromQuestion\": \"Q-5\",\n  \"fromSpan\": [\n   \"I-2\"\n  ],\n  \"id\": \"ASM-9\",\n  \"risk\": \"high\",\n  \"text\": \"How should customer users receive the one-time code required at sign-in? → assumed: Email and password, with a reset link by email; no social or single sign-on.\"\n },\n {\n  \"fromDefault\": \"notifications\",\n  \"fromQuestion\": \"Q-6\",\n  \"fromSpan\": [\n   \"I-2\",\n   \"I-3\"\n  ],\n  \"id\": \"ASM-10\",\n  \"risk\": \"low\",\n